# tools/font5x7_latin1_block_witness.rish -- the whole Latin-1 letter block, unified into one open font, proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) - font content for the open glyph atlas image/glyph.rye (gfa1). This is the finishing
# rung of the whole Latin-1 letter family, one level above the two partial unifiers already landed
# (tools/font5x7_accented_witness.rish gathered four lowercase accent corpora, tools/font5x7_upper_witness.rish gathered
# two uppercase accent corpora). Since those landed, the tree drew every remaining Latin-1 letter, until the block stood
# closed across thirteen leaf corpora. image/font5x7_latin1_block.rye gathers all thirteen into ONE gfa1 atlas.
#
# The crux this witness proves, beyond the round-trip and the ascending-and-unique disjointness the smaller unifiers prove,
# is BLOCK COMPLETENESS: every codepoint in U+00C0..U+00FF is present EXCEPT exactly the two that are not letters -- the
# multiplication sign U+00D7 and the division sign U+00F7, which live in image/font5x7_math.rye. The selftest walks the
# whole 64-codepoint block and proves each math sign misses while every other codepoint is present and carries the shared
# advance, so the font holds the whole letter block and nothing but it. The merged count equals the sum of the thirteen
# corpora (32 lowercase + 30 uppercase = 62), which with the strictly-ascending codepoints proves the corpora disjoint.
# Compression is reported as a fact, never asserted -- the round-trip is the proof. No network, no key, no funds -- the
# whole Latin-1 letter block a surface reads the day it spells any Western European name on our own open font.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/font5x7_latin1_block_witness.rish

say "font5x7-latin1-block: Language EN -- Season G font content; the whole Latin-1 Supplement letter block (sixty-two letters, every codepoint U+00C0..U+00FF but the two math signs) gathered from thirteen proven leaf corpora into one gfa1 atlas -- the whole Western European letter block in a single lookup."
say "font5x7-latin1-block: Style Radiant -- the thirteen corpora each already prove their own drawings on metal; this font merges their green atlases and proves the whole is block-complete, ascending, and disjoint, so decode(encode(atlas)) recovers every letter byte for byte; our own hand end to end, permissively ours, no external font to license and no web-search gate."
say "font5x7-latin1-block: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, u8 coverage bytes; every buffer names a maximum (cell_area - block_count - the atlas ceilings it rests on); the unifying count is the sum of the thirteen corpora's own count constants and equals the block's letter span; each function states its invariants positively; codepoints explicit and strictly ascending; the source stays plain ASCII; compression a reported fact never a false invariant; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/font5x7_latin1_block"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/font5x7_latin1_block.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "font5x7-latin1-block: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "font5x7-latin1-block: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "font5x7-latin1-block: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-font5x7-latin1-block" else "font5x7-latin1-block: selftest did not print the GREEN corpus line"
